From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:50:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: harden GRO boundaries and shared QDMA lifecycle

Select the missing checks from Gilly 975/977. Reject zero aggregate
counts and empty TCP payloads before allocating an SKB, and disable the
QDMA-wide GRO engine when the last QDMA user closes. The fanboy base no
longer shares HW GRO between QDMA users (a second open is refused while
it is enabled), so no peer feature synchronization is adjusted here.
Already-present GRO flags, high RX queues, aggregate upper bound and
nonzero timestamp guard are preserved.

Adapted-from: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com> (975) and
 Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org> (977)
Source: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18/tree/4b8fb8c3a2619dd239fb44fd511ee2848a07e768/openwrt-patches

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9999-zz-airoha-shared-qdma-gro.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9999-zz-airoha-shared-qdma-gro.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9999-zz-airoha-shared-qdma-gro.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:50:30 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] airoha: validate GRO aggregates and honor shared QDMA lifetime
+
+Select the missing checks from Gilly 975/977. Reject zero aggregate
+counts and empty TCP payloads before allocating an SKB, and disable the
+QDMA-wide GRO engine when the last QDMA user closes. The fanboy base no
+longer shares HW GRO between QDMA users (a second open is refused while
+it is enabled), so no peer feature synchronization is adjusted here.
+Already-present GRO flags, high RX queues, aggregate upper bound and
+nonzero timestamp guard are preserved.
+
+Adapted-from: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com> (975) and
+ Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org> (977)
+Source: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18/tree/4b8fb8c3a2619dd239fb44fd511ee2848a07e768/openwrt-patches
